// HarnessUpdateTrigger updates a trigger's mutable settings, including its name, status, prompt template, output configuration, session configuration, and schedule. Supply only the fields you want to change; `kind` and `webhook.provider` cannot be changed, and updating `session_template` replaces the stored template. Re-enabling a trigger does not produce a catch-up run, and schedule changes recompute `next_run_at`.
//
// Partial update: only the supplied fields change. `kind` and `webhook.provider` are immutable (409 on change). Mutable: `name` (409 on duplicate), `status` (active<->paused), `prompt_template`, `output`, `session_template` (fresh), `bound_session_id` (reuse), `cron.cron_expr` / `cron.timezone` (recomputes next_run_at). Re-enabling never produces a catch-up run. PATCHing session_template is a full replacement, so every spec.secrets slot value the new manifest declares must be resupplied (secret values are never echoed back), or the request is a 400.
//
// Parameters:
//
//	triggerId: The trigger UUID.
//	name: New team-unique trigger name. Same charset/length rules as create.
//	status: Trigger lifecycle state. Soft-deleted triggers are never returned
//	(404).
//	promptTemplate: Optional `string` value serialized in the `prompt_template`
//	wire field.
//	output: Output-delivery configuration on create/update. Exactly one of email
//	/ slack is required for the matching mode and forbidden otherwise;
//	destinations are stored encrypted and never returned.
//	sessionTemplate: fresh triggers only. A session_template PATCH is a full
//	replacement of the stored template; you must resupply every spec.secrets
//	slot value the new manifest declares, or the request is a 400.
//	boundSessionId: reuse triggers only. UUID of an existing session owned by
//	the team.
//	cron: cron block on create.
func (sdk *HarnessRuntimeNamespace) HarnessUpdateTrigger(ctx context.Context, params HarnessUpdateTriggerParams, opts ...RequestOption) (*GetTriggerResponse, error) {
	return HarnessUpdateTrigger(ctx, sdk.config, params, opts...)
}

